# Milestone: v0.10.10-job-introspection
# Covers: a failing arm of `&` or `,` stops its sibling arms and the block
#         that joins them, wherever in the join tree the failure happens.
# blocked: a failing `&` or `,` arm does not stop its sibling or the joining block; this tree lets the sibling run to completion.
# matrix-row: separator-detach
#
# The two legacy sections of tests/2.x/detach-error.chk that
# separator/detach-error.chk leaves out, copied below unaltered: the
# corner cases, and the checks that code is really stopped for `&` and
# `,` nodes.  On this tree `{ f, {x=0;sleep(100ms);x=1}}` leaves x at 1
# and `{ {x=0;x=4}& f}` leaves x at 4, where legacy asserts 0.  The
# diagnostics are the legacy `input.u:@.N: lookup failed: f` spelling,
# so activating this record also means re-spelling them as this core's
# `LookupError: slot access: slot 'f' not found`.
//corner cases
1 & f,
[00000022:error] !!! input.u:@.5: lookup failed: f
sleep(300ms);

f & 1,
[00000023:error] !!! input.u:@.1: lookup failed: f
sleep(300ms);

{1 & f} & 1,
[00000024:error] !!! input.u:@.6: lookup failed: f
sleep(300ms);

{f & 1} & 1,
[00000025:error] !!! input.u:@.2: lookup failed: f
sleep(300ms);

1 & {1 & f},
[00000026:error] !!! input.u:@.10: lookup failed: f
sleep(300ms);

1 & {f & 1},
[00000027:error] !!! input.u:@.6: lookup failed: f

// test that code is realy stopped for & and , nodes
x = 0|;

{ f, {x=0;sleep(100ms);x=1}};
[00000028:error] !!! input.u:@.3: lookup failed: f
assert { x == 0 };

{ {x=0;sleep(100ms);x=2}, f};
[00000030:error] !!! input.u:@.27: lookup failed: f
assert { x == 0 };

{ f& {x=0;x=3}};
[00000032:error] !!! input.u:@.3: lookup failed: f
assert { x == 0 };

{ {x=0;x=4}& f};
[00000034:error] !!! input.u:@.14: lookup failed: f
assert { x == 0 };
